{"availability":"available","full":"ifrederico/accessible-web-widget","name":"accessible-web-widget","description":"Script-tag accessibility preference widget with optional axe-core-powered dev checks.","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":17,"forks":11,"created":"2025-07-07T23:27:04Z","updated":"2026-10-03T04:08:57Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://accessibleweb.pages.dev/","topics":["a11y","accessibility","accessibility-widget","javascript","screen-reader","wcag","web-accessibility"],"demo":"https://accessibleweb.pages.dev/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T14:47:12.104Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T14:47:12.104Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T14:47:12.104Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T14:47:12.104Z","stars":17,"forks":11}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Most accessibility overlays promise to magically fix your site. This isn't that.","This is a small floating panel that gives your visitors controls they actually want — font sizing, contrast modes, a dyslexia-friendly font, animation pausing, text-to-speech, and more, in 54 languages. Think of it as the browser's built-in accessibility settings, just easier to find.","Real accessibility means semantic HTML, proper ARIA, keyboard navigation, and alt text baked into your code. No widget replaces that work. We support the Overlay Factsheet and built this as a complement, not a substitute. To find the issues actually worth fixing, run the companion Accessible Web Scanner over your sitemap."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ifrederico/accessible-web-widget/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"7907b9e8b654c6055d296906bc1d254c80b781a4fcd3bbaaa764ee3fb1c00d79","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T14:47:12.291Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T14:47:12.291Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Most accessibility overlays promise to magically fix your site. This isn't that.","sourceUrl":"https://gith